Lobium T-011 POC — native navigator.hardwareConcurrency override.

COMPILE-VERIFIED against Chromium 152.0.7928.0 (built on a 12-core machine, ~6.5h stock + ~2min
incremental). When launched with --lobium-hwc=<n>, navigator.hardwareConcurrency reports <n> instead
of the host CPU count — computed in C++ inside Blink, so there is NO JS-detectable tell (the exact
thing the interim patchright/CDP engine cannot do). Proven live: baseline HWC=12 -> --lobium-hwc=99
=> HWC=99 -> --lobium-hwc=4 => HWC=4.

This POC uses a single --lobium-hwc switch for minimal risk. The production path is the full config
channel (lobium/config-channel.md + lobium/src/lobium_fp_config.{h,cc} + engine-runner lobium-config.ts),
which feeds the whole Fingerprint via a per-profile JSON file; the same hook shape extends to the deep
surfaces (canvas/WebGL/audio) that ONLY native patching can spoof coherently.

Two hooks:
  1. content/browser/.../render_process_host_impl.cc — forward --lobium-hwc to the renderer process.
  2. third_party/blink/.../navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc — the getter reads the switch.

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
index ffdaf1716e..7774bdef8e 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
@@ -3826,6 +3826,7 @@ void RenderProcessHostImpl::PropagateBrowserCommandLineToRenderer(
   // Propagate the following switches to the renderer command line (along
   // with any associated values) if present in the browser command line.
   static const char* const kSwitchNames[] = {
+      "lobium-hwc",  // Lobium: forward the native fingerprint override to the renderer (T-011 POC)
       switches::kDisableInProcessStackTraces,
       sandbox::policy::switches::kDisableLandlockSandbox,
       sandbox::policy::switches::kDisableSeccompFilterSandbox,
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc
index f5c0db2d1b..2c95caa947 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc
@@ -4,11 +4,24 @@
 
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_concurrent_hardware.h"
 
+#include <cstdlib>
+
+#include "base/command_line.h"
 #include "base/system/sys_info.h"
 
 namespace blink {
 
 unsigned NavigatorConcurrentHardware::hardwareConcurrency() const {
+  // Lobium native fingerprint override (T-011 POC). When the orchestrator launches with
+  // --lobium-hwc=<n>, report that value instead of the host's real CPU count. Because this happens
+  // in C++ deep inside Blink, there is no JS-detectable tell (unlike the interim CDP/JS approach).
+  const base::CommandLine* cmd = base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess();
+  if (cmd->HasSwitch("lobium-hwc")) {
+    const int n = std::atoi(cmd->GetSwitchValueASCII("lobium-hwc").c_str());
+    if (n > 0) {
+      return static_cast<unsigned>(n);
+    }
+  }
   return static_cast<unsigned>(base::SysInfo::NumberOfProcessors());
 }
 
